    "collapsible_content_aqyrc4": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_jP3dUU": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does a typical training day look like?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The morning session will predominately focus on the theory required to test and tag, while the afternoon focuses heavily on learning to actually test and tag with a portable appliance tester. All of our classes are kept to a maximum of 12 people so that everyone in the room can get individual time and support from our trainer. Upon completing the course, you should be completely comfortable at testing and tagging on your own. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_9amYtn": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is the Nationally Recognised course different to the Short course? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Both the Nationally Recognised and Short Courses are delivered in a face-to-face training session over 1 day. However, the major difference between them is that the Nationally Recognised Course has an additional self-paced OHS (Occupational Health and Safety) online component and is thereby considered the highest qualification (ASQA approved). The course you decide on will largely depend on your particular needs, but most students will complete the Nationally Recognised one for <a href=\"/pages/choosing-right-course\" title=\"Which Test & Tag Course Should I Choose?\">various reasons</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_xbHAmB": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where in Victoria are classes held?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We offer two convenient training centres across Melbourne. </p><p>Our newly renovated, state-of-the-art head office is located in Rowville at 8 Mosrael Place, just off Stud Road and minutes from the Eastern Freeway. With ample on-site parking and top-tier training facilities, it’s designed to provide the best learning experience. Plus, we have a full range of PAT Testers available for hands-on practice with the model of your choice.</p><p>Our second location is in Caroline Springs, situated on Caroline Springs Boulevard at the Punthill Apartments, offering a convenient option for those in the western suburbs.</p><p>Alternatively, we can provide onsite training at your venue if you have a group who require training. Please contact our friendly team on <a href=\"tel:1300848302\" title=\"tel:1300848302\">1300 848 302</a> and they'll be more than happy to help.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YAFc4k": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does the course go for? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our Test & Tag Course in Rowville and Caroline Springs generally starts at 8:00 am and finishes at approximately 4:30 pm, with breaks for morning tea and lunch. If you’re planning on doing the Nationally Recognised course, it’ll consist of an additional self-paced WHS component, which is to be completed in your own time before the course date. This typically takes around 3-4 hours to complete, depending on your existing knowledge. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wgai4y": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I need technical support or help after the course? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>You’ll have the peace of mind knowing that we'll be there when you need us, whether it's by phone, email or in person. Every single student taught by Test & Tag Training receives free lifetime technical support from our team of experts. Guaranteed. </p><p>This could be anything from how to use a specific appliance tester or how to test and tag a particular electrical appliance. We want to ensure we're making people's jobs easier by offering dependable service and expert advice when you need it most.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DhYd67": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who will be the instructor on the day? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Test & Tag Training in Victoria are led by Mark Juric, one of our highly experienced instructors with over 20 years of experience in the electrotechnology industry. With a strong background in teaching and a deep understanding of Australia test and tag standards, Mark brings a huge amount of knowledge to each class. We guarantee that Mark will give you all the knowledge and skills required to successfully test and tag on your own.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
